    Development Goal
    In order to address the core problem in the district, the participants formulated an overall
    development goal for the district as follows:
    To strengthen the local Government administration, improve the agricultural and livestock
    production levels and quality, and to provide access to basic infrastructure and social services
    throughout the district.
    Development Objectives and Strategies
    In order to achieve the overall development goal, the participants set three development
    objectives for the district and recommended strategies for achieving those objectives.
    Objective One
    To improve agricultural and livestock production levels and quality in the district.
    Major Strategies
    1. Construction of new and restoration of existing irrigation systems such as canals, karizes,
    river dykes and brooks.
    2. Improvement of the agricultural and livestock production levels and quality.
    3. Establishment of veterinary clinics and provision of pesticides and other plant and animal
    disease prevention remedies.
    Objective Two
    To provide better access to new, restored and improved social services such as education,
    healthcare and social protection.
    Major Strategies
    1. Establishment of well-regulated health centres in the district with provision of essential
    medical equipment, supplies and medicines.
    2. Improvement of local education standards with provisions of essential education equipment
    and supplies and capacity building programmes for local teachers and education personnel.
    3. Development of an effective social protection and welfare system in the district.
    Objective Three
    To provide access to basic infrastructure services such as roads, bridges, culverts and reliable
    and affordable source of public electricity.
    Major Strategies
    1. Construction of new roads, bridges and culverts, and asphalting and gravelling of existing
    roads in the district.
    2. Construction of public power generation stations throughout the district.
    Prioritized Project Ideas
    After having developed strategies and activities, the participants identified and prioritized 50
    project ideas to achieve the development goals for the district, five of which were specifically
    proposed by female participants. It is expected that these priority project ideas will be discussed
    in a provincial development planning process to ensure that community priority needs are
    articulated in the Government’s provincial and national development plans.
